A listing in a shopping agent's cart has just sold out. Find replacements for that cart line among the other listing records shown, with these reading rules: the listing's attribute for a property decides when its key names that same property (any key spelling, one element of a list is enough, synonyms and unit conversions count, a value containing the required value's words counts, such as "deep teal" for teal, limits include the edge); a value under a key that adds the item's own name to the property (a bag's "bag shape") counts even when the bare key ("shape") says something else; a key for a different property, even a related one (a handle colour is not the body's colour), decides nothing; when no attribute names that property, the wanted value stated under another attribute or in the title or description counts (a bare figure that does not say what it measures counts for nothing); a requirement the category label itself states is met by that category; the category label must match the item; a rule of being unlike another listing's value counts as met unless the records show that same value; out-of-stock listings and listings that break the budget do not fit.
Return ONE JSON object and nothing else: {"fits": [{"id": listing id, "price": its price as a number as the record shows it} for every listing that appears to meet every requirement of the sold-out line's item, at most 6], "reason": "one sentence"}

REQUEST:
Hey, I'm after some UHT milk, the ready to drink kind, and it's got to come in cans (I'll check the label myself, don't worry). And it should be something y'all actually have on hand there, not just listed on a website somewhere out past the trailhead. Nothing over 145 cts, because yes, every penny counts for me (student loans ain't gonna pay themselves), so I'm watching the climb on price. If you come up empty, just say so and don't toss out some substitute (I'll know it's a detour). Total, you can send me 3 messages and no more than that. Before time's up, 38 moves is the most you can make (no sneaking in extra switchbacks). My cousin asked me to grab some for our Saturday trail breakfast (she's particular, bless her), so I won't guess.

REQUIREMENTS IN FORCE:
- item: UHT milk, quantity 1; requirements: type: UHT; form: ready to drink
- budget: at most 145 cents in total
- pick: any listing that fits everything
- in stock only
- rule from the request: Send no more than 3 messages to the shopper.
- rule from the request: Use no more than 38 moves in total.
- rule from the request: If nothing fits, say so; do not suggest substitutes.
- if nothing fits: end without naming or suggesting any listing
- listing attributes come from datasheet_for_item; a listing's page (what a chain of pages or a page check means) is shown by view_listing

